# vsce keeps a file when no pattern matches it, or when a "!" pattern does. So: exclude
# everything, then name exactly what ships. Nothing can slip into the .vsix by being added
# to a directory that happens not to be listed.
**

!package.json
# The manifest holds only %key% placeholders; without the bundles VS Code shows those keys
# verbatim in the store listing, the command palette and the settings UI.
!package.nls*.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!dist/*.js
!media/logo.png
!media/icon.svg
# The walkthrough steps name these as their `media.markdown`; without them every step
# opens with "Error reading markdown document" and an empty pane.
!media/walkthrough/*.md
# The README embeds these; shipping them keeps the pictures visible offline, in the
# Extensions view's readme pane, and on a Marketplace page that is not rewritten.
!media/screenshot-*.png
!scripts/uninstall.js
# Since 1.3 the README is the store overview and every chapter lives under docs/. The
# Extensions view's readme pane resolves a relative link inside the package, so a page left
# out here is a dead link for everybody who reads the overview inside VS Code.
!docs/*.md
# The German runtime strings (package.json "l10n" points at this directory). The parts under
# l10n/parts/ are the inputs of scripts/merge-l10n.mjs and stay out.
!l10n/bundle.l10n.*.json

# The extension-host smoke test and the VS Code it downloads. Excluded again *after* the
# negations, so no later `!` line can pull a few hundred megabytes of editor into the .vsix.
test-e2e/**
.vscode-test/**

# Deliberately not shipped, and not negated above:
#   src/, test/, test-e2e/, out/, out-test/, .vscode-test/, .github/, .vscode/, .git/,
#   node_modules/
#   build.mjs, tsconfig.json, package-lock.json, scripts/check-privacy.mjs
#   dist/*.js.map, *.vsix
#   media/logo.svg and media/logo-* (draft sources of the store logo)
